            <div class="note amber">
              <div class="note-label">🎯 Benefits of TypeScript</div>

              <ul>
                <li><strong>🐛 Catches bugs early</strong> - Type errors are caught while coding, not at runtime</li>
                <li><strong>📝 Better autocomplete</strong> - Your editor knows what properties exist on objects</li>
                <li><strong>🔄 Easier refactoring</strong> - Change an interface, TypeScript tells you everywhere that needs updating</li>
                <li><strong>📖 Self-documenting code</strong> - Types tell you what data functions expect and return</li>
                <li><strong>🏗️ Better for large teams</strong> - Types act as contracts between developers</li>
                <li><strong>🔧 Modern JavaScript features</strong> - Use future JS features today (compiled to older JS for browser support)</li>
