          <!-- BLOCK 4: Pros and Cons of SPA                 -->
          <!-- ============================================= -->
          <div class="block">
            <h3>Pros and Cons of SPAs</h3>

            <div class="note green">
              <div class="note-label">✅ Advantages of SPAs (Angular)</div>

              <ul>
                <li><strong>⚡ Faster navigation</strong> - No page reloads, instant transitions</li>
                <li><strong>💾 State preservation</strong> - Data stays in memory while navigating (e.g., unsaved form data, scroll position)</li>
                <li><strong>📱 App-like experience</strong> - Feels like a native mobile/desktop app</li>
                <li><strong>🌐 Less server load</strong> - Server serves static files once, then just JSON data</li>
                <li><strong>🔄 Easier caching</strong> - Core app can be cached, only data changes</li>
                <li><strong>📦 Smaller bandwidth after first load</strong> - Subsequent navigations only fetch JSON (much smaller than HTML)</li>
                <li><strong>🎨 Rich interactions</strong> - Animations, transitions, real-time updates are easier</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="note red">
              <div class="note-label">❌ Disadvantages of SPAs</div>

              <ul>
                <li><strong>🐌 Slower initial load</strong> - Must download entire app framework before showing anything</li>
                <li><strong>🔍 SEO challenges</strong> - Search engines struggle with JavaScript-rendered content (solved with Angular Universal/SSR)</li>
                <li><strong>📊 Analytics complexity</strong> - Need to manually track page views (router events)</li>
                <li><strong>🔗 Link sharing issues</strong> - Without proper routing setup, deep links may break</li>
                <li><strong>🧠 Memory management</strong> - Developers must manually unsubscribe to prevent memory leaks</li>
                <li><strong>🕸️ Accessibility concerns</strong> - Need to manage focus, announce route changes to screen readers</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

