              <ul>
                <li><strong>SPA (Angular):</strong> One HTML file, JavaScript handles routing, no page reloads, feels like an app</li>
                <li><strong>MPA (Traditional):</strong> Multiple HTML files, server generates each page, full reloads on every navigation</li>
                <li><strong>First load trade-off:</strong> SPA is slower first load, faster subsequent navigation. MPA is faster first load, slower subsequent navigation.</li>
                <li><strong>Angular Router</strong> is the magic that enables SPA navigation without reloads</li>
                <li><strong>SEO can be solved</strong> with Angular Universal (SSR) or prerendering</li>
                <li><strong>SPA is best for</strong> web applications, dashboards, tools, e-commerce</li>
                <li><strong>MPA is best for</strong> blogs, news sites, content-heavy sites with SEO as priority</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="note green">
