          <div class="block">
            <h3>Best Practices</h3>

            <div class="note red">
              <div class="note-label">📖 Service Best Practices Summary</div>

              <ul>
                <li><strong>Keep components focused on UI</strong> - Components handle templates, events, user interaction</li>
                <li><strong>Move reusable logic into services</strong> - Don't duplicate code across components</li>
                <li><strong>Use services for API communication</strong> - All HTTP calls belong in services</li>
                <li><strong>Expose Observables instead of raw subjects</strong> - Use .asObservable() to prevent external .next() calls</li>
                <li><strong>Avoid business logic inside templates</strong> - Complex calculations go in services</li>
                <li><strong>Use one service for one responsibility</strong> - UserService handles users, ProductService handles products</li>
                <li><strong>Always use providedIn: 'root' for singletons</strong> - Unless you need a new instance per component</li>
                <li><strong>Unsubscribe from subscriptions</strong> - Use takeUntil or async pipe to prevent memory leaks</li>
                <li><strong>Test services independently</strong> - Services are easier to test than components</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="note green">
              <div class="note-label">🎯 Quick Reference: Component vs Service</div>

