            <p>A <code>BehaviorSubject</code> is both an Observable AND an Observer. It stores the current value and immediately emits it to any new subscriber. This is the standard pattern for shared state in Angular services.</p>

            <div class="note purple">
              <div class="note-label">📖 Detailed Explanation: BehaviorSubject</div>

              <p><strong>Problem with Regular Observables:</strong> If you subscribe LATE, you miss previous values!</p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript"><span class="cm">// Regular Observable - late subscribers miss data</span>
      <span class="kw">const</span> numbers$ = of(<span class="num">1</span>, <span class="num">2</span>, <span class="num">3</span>);
      numbers$.subscribe(v => console.log(<span class="str">'Subscriber 1:'</span>, v));  <span class="cm">// Gets 1, 2, 3</span>
