              <p><strong>How switchMap works:</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li>User types "a" → Request A starts</li>
                <li>User types "an" (before Request A finishes) → Request A is CANCELLED, Request B starts</li>
                <li>User types "ang" (before Request B finishes) → Request B is CANCELLED, Request C starts</li>
                <li>User stops typing → Only the final request completes → Correct results!</li>
              </ul>

              <div class="note red">
                <div class="note-label">⚠️ Important!</div>
                <p>switchMap CANCELS previous HTTP requests. This is good for search (only last result matters), but BAD for things where every request matters (like saving form data). For saving, use mergeMap or concatMap instead!</p>
