              <p><strong>4 Types of Data Binding:</strong></p>

              <p><strong>1. Interpolation (component → template):</strong> <code>{{ variableName }}</code> displays the variable's current value.</p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript">name = "John";</pre>
              <pre data-lang="html">&lt;h1&gt;Hello {{ name }}!&lt;/h1&gt;  <span class="cm">// Shows "Hello John!"</span></pre>

              <p><strong>2. Property Binding (component → template):</strong> <code>[property]="variable"</code> sets HTML properties dynamically.</p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript">isDisabled = true;</pre>
              <pre data-lang="html">&lt;button [disabled]="isDisabled"&gt;Click Me&lt;/button&gt;  <span class="cm">// Button is disabled!</span></pre>

              <p><strong>3. Event Binding (template → component):</strong> <code>(event)="method()"</code> calls component methods when user interacts.</p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript">saveData() { console.log("Saved!"); }</pre>
              <pre data-lang="html">&lt;button (click)="saveData()"&gt;Save&lt;/button&gt;  <span class="cm">// Clicks call saveData()</span></pre>

              <p><strong>4. Two-Way Binding (component ↔ template):</strong> <code>[(ngModel)]="variable"</code> syncs both ways.</p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript">username = "";</pre>
              <pre data-lang="html">&lt;input [(ngModel)]="username"&gt;  <span class="cm">// User types → variable updates</span>
      &lt;p&gt;You typed: {{ username }}&lt;/p&gt;  <span class="cm">// Variable updates → display updates</span></pre>
              <p><strong>This is called "banana in a box"</strong> because the syntax looks like <code>[()]</code> - a banana (parentheses) in a box (brackets)!</p>
            </div>
          </div>

