          <div class="block">
            <h3># Routing & HTTP Client</h3>
            <p>Routing changes views without reloading page. Router outlet: <code>&lt;router-outlet&gt;&lt;/router-outlet&gt;</code>.</p>
            <p>HttpClient communicates with servers (APIs return JSON). Real flow: User opens page → Router loads component → Component asks Service → Service calls API → Server returns JSON → Component updates UI.</p>

            <div class="note blue">
              <div class="note-label">📖 Detailed Explanation</div>
              <p><strong>Routing - How navigation works in SPA:</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li>Traditional websites: Click link → Browser asks server for new HTML file → Server sends it → Page reloads (white screen)</li>
                <li>Angular SPA: Click link → Router intercepts click (stops browser) → Router changes URL in address bar → Router shows different component in &lt;router-outlet&gt; → No page reload!</li>
              </ul>

              <p><strong>Setting up routes:</strong></p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript"><span class="kw">const</span> routes = [
        { path: <span class="str">'home'</span>, component: HomeComponent },     <span class="cm">// /home shows HomeComponent</span>
        { path: <span class="str">'about'</span>, component: AboutComponent },   <span class="cm">// /about shows AboutComponent</span>
        { path: <span class="str">''</span>, redirectTo: <span class="str">'home'</span> }                <span class="cm">// empty URL goes to home</span>
      ];</pre>

              <p><strong>Router outlet placement:</strong> Wherever you put <code>&lt;router-outlet&gt;</code>, that's where routed components appear. Usually in app.component.html between header and footer.</p>

              <p><strong>HTTP Client - Getting data from servers:</strong></p>
              <pre data-lang="typescript"><span class="cm">// In a service</span>
      <span class="kw">constructor</span>(<span class="kw">private</span> http: HttpClient) {}

      getUsers() {
        <span class="kw">return</span> this.http.get(<span class="str">'https://api.example.com/users'</span>);
      }

      <span class="cm">// In a component</span>
      ngOnInit() {
        this.userService.getUsers().subscribe(users => {
          this.users = users;  <span class="cm">// Data arrives here (async)</span>
        });
      }</pre>

              <p><strong>Complete data flow example:</strong></p>
