              <p><strong>SEO (Search Engine Optimization):</strong> Making your app appear higher in Google search results. SPA traditionally struggle with SEO because search engines have trouble with JavaScript content. SSR solves this.</p>

              <p><strong>Server Side Rendering (SSR) vs Client Side Rendering (CSR):</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>CSR (normal Angular):</strong> Browser loads empty HTML, then JavaScript runs, then content appears. Slower first load, worse SEO.</li>
                <li><strong>SSR (Angular Universal):</strong> Server generates complete HTML with content, sends to browser. Content appears immediately! Better SEO, faster perceived performance.</li>
              </ul>

              <p><strong>Real-Life Analogy (Restaurant):</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Component = Waiter</strong> - Interacts with customer (user), takes orders (events), brings food (UI). Should not cook (no business logic).</li>
