            <h3>Animation Performance Tips</h3>

            <div class="note red">
              <div class="note-label">⚡ Performance Best Practices</div>

              <ul>
                <li><strong>✅ Use transform and opacity</strong> - These are GPU-accelerated and smooth</li>
                <li><strong>❌ Avoid animating layout properties</strong> - width, height, margin, padding (cause repaints)</li>
                <li><strong>✅ Use will-change CSS property</strong> - Hint browser about what will animate</li>
                <li><strong>✅ Keep animations short</strong> - 200-400ms is ideal for most UI animations</li>
                <li><strong>❌ Avoid animating too many elements at once</strong> - Can cause jank</li>
                <li><strong>✅ Use requestAnimationFrame for custom animations</strong> - Syncs with browser refresh rate</li>
              </ul>

              <pre data-lang="scss"><span class="cm">// CSS performance hints</span>
      .animated-element {
        will-change: transform, opacity;  <span class="cm">// Tell browser what will animate</span>
      }

      <span class="cm">// ❌ Bad - Animates layout (causes repaints)</span>
      .bad-animation {
        transition: width 300ms, height 300ms, margin 300ms;
      }

      <span class="cm">// ✅ Good - Animates transform (GPU accelerated)</span>
      .good-animation {
        transition: transform 300ms, opacity 300ms;
      }</pre>
